    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d715">

                <pb facs="0596" n="480" xml:id="pg480"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/11595.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Canada to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-21T17:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 21, 1914, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Captain <hi rendition="#italic">Ypiranga</hi> has placed himself subject orders
                    Admiral Fletcher and delivered bills of lading, which show munitions of war as
                    reported. He agrees not to leave his position unless driven away by storm and
                    then will remain within reach of guns our ships.</p>
                <p>Our men are firing now only when fired at. We prepared flag of truce with message
                    to General Maas to cease firing or our big guns will be used. Now about one
                    thousand marines and blue jackets ashore. Admiral Badger with heavy force due
                    here tonight. All business here suspended since noon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canada</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
